      "seed": 708393586,
      "version": 534,
      "versionNonce": 1208314845,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779808166767,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "this is one of the simpliest way of implementation\nlocation base search is handled by db itself.\n\nhow searching works?\n\nWhen a restaurant, hotel, or driver is added to our application, we store its location (lat and long) in the database\nThe location field is a special GIS field\nNow when user searches for nearby restaurants, we do not need to manually check grids or tree nodes\n“Give me all restaurants within 5 km of this user location.”\nPostGIS provides built-in functions for this.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "this is one of the simpliest way of implementation\nlocation base search is handled by db itself.\n\nhow searching works?\n\nWhen a restaurant, hotel, or driver is added to our application, we store its location (lat and long) in the database\nThe location field is a special GIS field\nNow when user searches for nearby restaurants, we do not need to manually check grids or tree nodes\n“Give me all restaurants within 5 km of this user location.”\nPostGIS provides built-in functions for this.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
