      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779808166767,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "for large scale application like uber zomato rapido the search is base on location (lat and long) it this case always go with Geo Hash approach. its best for those type of things\n\nif search is not just limited to location (lat and long) we also have feature of search using text then either of one is fine (postgress with gis or elastic search)\ncoz if user is writting anyting like nameof location we alsohave to make sure to handle fuzzy words. thats why ES or Postgress (GIS and Fuzztstrmatch) is best for that.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "for large scale application like uber zomato rapido the search is base on location (lat and long) it this case always go with Geo Hash approach. its best for those type of things\n\nif search is not just limited to location (lat and long) we also have feature of search using text then either of one is fine (postgress with gis or elastic search)\ncoz if user is writting anyting like nameof location we alsohave to make sure to handle fuzzy words. thats why ES or Postgress (GIS and Fuzztstrmatch) is best for that.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
